### C: Dynamically Link NGSPICE DLL at Runtime

Source: https://github.com/pyspice-org/pyspice/blob/master/examples/c-examples/ngspice_cb/ngspice_cb_contents.txt

This conceptual C code snippet demonstrates how to dynamically load 'ngspice.dll' at runtime using Windows API functions like `LoadLibrary` and `GetProcAddress`. This method allows the application to link to the DLL without requiring it at compile time, making the executable more flexible. It requires defining function pointer types matching the DLL's exported functions.

```C
// ng_shared_test/main.c (Conceptual for Dynamic Linking)
#include <stdio.h>
#include <windows.h> // Required for LoadLibrary, GetProcAddress, FreeLibrary

// Function pointer types matching ngspice.dll exports
typedef int (*ngSpice_Init_ptr)(void*, void*, void*, void*, void*, void*, void*);
typedef int (*ngSpice_Command_ptr)(char*);

// Example callback function for NGSPICE messages
int ngspice_sendChar_callback(char* msg) {
    printf("NGSPICE Output: %s\n", msg);
    return 0;
}

int main() {
    HMODULE hNgspiceDll = NULL;
    ngSpice_Init_ptr p_ngSpice_Init = NULL;
    ngSpice_Command_ptr p_ngSpice_Command = NULL;

    // Load the ngspice.dll library
    hNgspiceDll = LoadLibrary("ngspice.dll");
    if (hNgspiceDll == NULL) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Error: Could not load ngspice.dll. Make sure it's in the PATH or same directory.\n");
        return 1;
    }

    // Get function pointers for required NGSPICE functions
    p_ngSpice_Init = (ngSpice_Init_ptr)GetProcAddress(hNgspiceDll, "ngSpice_Init");
    p_ngSpice_Command = (ngSpice_Command_ptr)GetProcAddress(hNgspiceDll, "ngSpice_Command");

    if (p_ngSpice_Init && p_ngSpice_Command) {
        printf("NGSPICE DLL loaded successfully. Initializing...\n");
        // Initialize NGSPICE with callback functions
        p_ngSpice_Init(ngspice_sendChar_callback, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);

        // Execute NGSPICE commands
        p_ngSpice_Command("source my_circuit.cir");
        p_ngSpice_Command("run");
        p_ngSpice_Command("quit");
    } else {
        fprintf(stderr, "Error: Could not find NGSPICE functions in DLL.\n");
    }

    // Unload the DLL
    FreeLibrary(hNgspiceDll);
    printf("NGSPICE DLL unloaded.\n");
    return 0;
}
```

### Custom Hook for Data Fetching with useQuery

Source: https://github.com/tanstack/query/blob/main/examples/react/nextjs/src/hooks/usePosts.ts

A reusable custom hook pattern that wraps useQuery with a typed fetch function and parameterized query key. Demonstrates the standard pattern for encapsulating data fetching logic into a custom hook with co-located queryKey and queryFn.

```typescript
import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/react-query'

type Post = {
  id: number
  title: string
  body: string
}

const fetchPosts = async (limit = 10): Promise<Array<Post>> => {
  const response = await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts')
  const data = await response.json()
  return data.filter((x: Post) => x.id <= limit)
}

const usePosts = (limit: number) => {
  return useQuery({
    queryKey: ['posts', limit],
    queryFn: () => fetchPosts(limit),
  })
}

export { usePosts, fetchPosts }
```

