### Configure TanStack Query for SSR in Remix

Source: https://github.com/tanstack/query/blob/main/docs/framework/react/guides/ssr.md

This example illustrates how to set up `QueryClientProvider` in the `app/root.tsx` file for Remix applications. Similar to Next.js, initializing the `QueryClient` within `React.useState` guarantees a unique instance per request, which is vital for maintaining data isolation and optimal performance in SSR. It also includes a default `staleTime` configuration to prevent unnecessary client-side refetches.

```tsx
// app/root.tsx
import { Outlet } from '@remix-run/react'
import { QueryClient, QueryClientProvider } from '@tanstack/react-query'

export default function MyApp() {
  const [queryClient] = React.useState(
    () =>
      new QueryClient({
        defaultOptions: {
          queries: {
            // With SSR, we usually want to set some default staleTime
            // above 0 to avoid refetching immediately on the client
            staleTime: 60 * 1000,
          },
        },
      }),
  )

  return (
    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>
      <Outlet />
    </QueryClientProvider>
  )
}
```

