### Initialize Xyce for Embedded Use (C++)

Source: https://context7.com/xyce/xyce/llms.txt

Shows a two-phase initialization process for embedding Xyce within other applications. This involves creating a Simulator instance with an MPI communicator, preparing arguments, performing an 'initializeEarly' step to read the netlist, an 'initializeLate' step for setup, and finally running the simulation.

```cpp
// Two-phase initialization for embedded applications
#include <N_CIR_Xyce.h>
#include <vector>
#include <string>

// Create simulator with MPI communicator
Xyce::Circuit::Simulator xyce(MPI_COMM_WORLD);

// Prepare command-line arguments (without "Xyce" as arg 0)
std::vector<std::string> arguments;
arguments.push_back("circuit.cir");
arguments.push_back("-l");
arguments.push_back("logfile.txt");

// First phase: read netlist and instantiate devices
Xyce::Circuit::Simulator::RunStatus status = xyce.initializeEarly(arguments);
if (status != Xyce::Circuit::Simulator::SUCCESS) {
  std::cerr << "Early initialization failed" << std::endl;
  return 1;
}

// Second phase: setup topology and matrix structures
status = xyce.initializeLate();
if (status != Xyce::Circuit::Simulator::SUCCESS) {
  std::cerr << "Late initialization failed" << std::endl;
  return 1;
}

// Run the simulation
status = xyce.runSimulation();
if (status != Xyce::Circuit::Simulator::SUCCESS) {
  std::cerr << "Simulation failed" << std::endl;
  return 1;
}
```

