### Run Basic Xyce Simulation (C++)

Source: https://context7.com/xyce/xyce/llms.txt

Demonstrates how to run a basic Xyce simulation directly from the main entry point. This requires including the necessary Xyce headers and instantiating the Simulator class. The 'run' method takes command-line arguments similar to how Xyce is invoked from the terminal.

```cpp
#include <N_CIR_Xyce.h>
#include <N_ERH_ErrorMgr.h>

int main(int argc, char *argv[]) {
  bool bsuccess = false;

  // Create Xyce simulator instance
  Xyce::Circuit::Simulator xyce;

  // Run simulation with command-line arguments
  // Expected: Xyce circuit.cir
  bsuccess = xyce.run(argc, argv);

  if (!bsuccess) {
    Xyce::Circuit::Xyce_exit(1, false);
  }

  return 0;
}
```

